source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A marker run on the line the cell continues onto opens a list there: Jira renders one data cell holding `a`, a forced newline, and a round list with the one item `item`. jiro reads the row across both lines and keeps the whole table as raw Jira Markup, which a GFM cell could hold none of.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|a\\
* item|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />
<ul>
	<li>item</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||
|a\\
* item|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
